  "text": "Recipe: Daal Chaat\nCreator: Kiran Sharma\nCategory: Chaat\nIngredients: Masoor daal (whole, skinless), Split Moong daal, Hing powder (asafoetida), Haldi powder (turmeric powder), Himalayan salt, Water, Roasted jeera powder (roasted cumin powder), Amchoor powder (dry mango powder), Chaat Masala, Black pepper powder, Chopped onions, Chopped tomatoes, Green chilies, Pomegranate seeds, Microgreens, Cilantro, Tamarind Chutney, Mint Chutney, Purple sweet potato, Ezekiel crisps, Lemon, Cucumber, Sweet corn, Bell pepper\nCooking methods: boil, whisk, bake, no-cook\nInstructions: **DAAL:** Boil Masoor daal (whole, skinless) or Split Moong daal (soaked for 4-5 hours) with Hing powder (asafoetida), Haldi powder (turmeric powder), Himalayan salt, and Water in a pressure cooker for 2 whistles. Then whisk to puree consistency.\n**DRY MASALA:** Mix Roasted jeera powder (roasted cumin powder), Amchoor powder (dry mango powder), Chaat Masala, and Black pepper powder together in a bowl.\n**ASSEMBLY:** Serve daal in a bowl. Add toppings of your choice (Chopped onions, Chopped tomatoes, Green chilies, Pomegranate seeds, Microgreens, Cilantro, Tamarind Chutney, Mint Chutney, Purple sweet potato). Crush Ezekiel crisps and add. Garnish with cilantro. Squeeze some lemon juice. Daal Chaat is ready!\nNotes: Ezekiel crisps: bake Ezekiel 4:9 tortillas in a pre-heated oven at 410 F. They turn crispy in 5-6 mins.",
